  "uncertain": [
    "The individual contacts of the 2-pin LED connectors and the JST power connector are not drawn distinctly; which contact carries '5V Out' vs the 'In' signal (and 5V IN vs GND) is inferred from the stacking/placement of the callout labels beside each connector.",
    "LED output 1 sits level with the USB-C connector, so 'end closest to USB' is marginal for it; bottom-first was applied to all six LED connectors for consistency."
  ],
  "notes": "Image 2 is the same Pins and Dims artwork at a smaller size; transcribed separately per rule 11. Numbers before PWM/I2C/UART names are the peripheral index per the image key (e.g. '0 SDA' = I2C0 SDA, '4 B' = PWM slice 4 channel B). On-board silkscreen marks (+, S, -, 5V) are listed first in functions. ADC column for GP26 shows '0'."
